      "content": "thanks for that. so when you talk about \"differing expectations regarding public behavior\" or \"challenges to the established neighborhood character,\" aren't you basically saying that these specific groups often bring certain behaviors that are fundamentally at odds with Western middle-class stability? i'm trying to figure out if there's a pattern where certain ethnicities are statistically more likely to cause this kind of \"friction\" or social decay in these types of areas.",
